    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Trea Turner** (79.76) headlining the lineup as elite plays. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from the matchup against Shane Baz; his speed profile is perfectly suited to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, and with favorable park factors adding 16% to his projection, he is a primary source for our scarcest category, stolen bases. Similarly, **Trea Turner** draws a high-leverage spot atop the order against Andrew Abbott. Abbott\u2019s 5.07 xERA suggests the environment is ripe for **Trea Turner** to capitalize on his dynamic platoon advantage, while **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41) also benefits from the same matchup, maintaining a strong profile as a power-heavy utility option in the outfield.\n\nWhile our core is solidified, we are closely monitoring the 44% rain risk in the game involving **Pedro Ramirez** (60.72) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Should that matchup be postponed, we would need to pivot to the bench, where **Nelson Velazquez** (55.26) sits as the primary contingency. **Nelson Velazquez** was the closest cut from the starting nine; while his 0.418 xwOBA is elite, the optimizer favored the higher volume and batting order stability currently projected for **Carson Benge** (55.45) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (52.14). Elsewhere, we are cautious with **Yordan Alvarez** (52.37), whose raw power remains dangerous, but his score is suppressed today by a challenging L/L matchup against Andrew Alvarez, resulting in a -19% penalty based on SP skill and platoon dynamics. We will look to **Colt Keith** (64.98) and **Junior Caminero** (62.52) to provide the necessary floor and RBI production required to navigate a day where pitching matchups are largely favorable across the board.",
